Structural records: literals, canonical field order, getters/setters as values, nesting.
$[Import* std]
$[# a {. y 2 x 1}]
$[# b {. x 1 y 2}]
${= a b} $a
expect: true
expect: {x: 1, y: 2}
$[# c {.x= a 5}]
$a $c
expect: {x: 1, y: 2}
expect: {x: 5, y: 2}
$[# l {. from a tags {' "red"}}]
${.y {.from l}} ${.tags l}
expect: 2
expect: ["red"]
${. } ${= {hash a} {hash b}}
expect: {}
expect: true
Getters and setters are ordinary functions with row-polymorphic types:
${map {' a c} .x} ${map {' a c} {^ {r} {.y= r 0}}}
expect: [1, 5]
expect: [{x: 1, y: 0}, {x: 5, y: 0}]
$[# getX .x]
${getX {. x "s" z true}} ${getX a}
expect: "s"
expect: 1
A computed Struct type checks a literal by ascription:
$[# P [% {Struct {' {Field "x" Int} {Field "y" Int}}}]]
${: {. y 1 x 2} P}
expect: {x: 2, y: 1}
Fields are evaluated in source order:
$[# trace [% {. second {length {' 1 2}} first {length {'}}}]]
$trace
expect: {first: 0, second: 2}
